<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vijayanagara Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1336</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vijayanagara Empire was a powerful <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> state in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> founded around 1336, with its capital at Vijayanagara on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tungabhadra-river">Tungabhadra River</a>. It arose as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> control over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> and the south weakened. The Delhi Sultanate profile treats its emergence as a sign of the sultanate's decline, and it dominated much of southern India until its defeat in 1565.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire.jpg" alt="Vijayanagara Empire" width="320" height="269" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Avantiputra7 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vijayanagara_Empire_c.1485.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
